=== TEST_DESIGN ===
Reflective coverage assertion over protomodel.Signals (codegen output).

Three invariants enforced from the protomodel side, redundant with
loader-side checks where they overlap so a regression in one layer
still leaves the other as a backstop:

  1. Coverage  - every Signal where IsCompound==false has at least
                  one entry in rt.LoadMap(). Catches a re-vendored
                  proto that adds a SignalMeta and forgets the
                  matching routing.yaml entry.
  2. Uniqueness- every Signal name is referenced by at most one
                  routing entry. (Loader's validateEntries already
                  rejects this from the YAML side; the seen-counter
                  here is the protomodel-side mirror.)
  3. No orphans- every routing entry name resolves to either
                  pm.SignalsByName (atomic Field, or compound parent
                  whose codec flattener emits under its own name)
                  OR is a strict prefix-extension of a compound
                  parent name (flattened child like LocationLatitude,
                  TpmsHardWarningsFrontLeft, DoorStateDriverFront).

Compound handling:
  pm.Signals lists 8 compounds (Location, OriginLocation,
  DestinationLocation, DoorState, TpmsHardWarnings, TpmsSoftWarnings,
  ScheduledChargingStartTime, ScheduledDepartureTime). The codec at
  internal/tesla/codec/flatten.go expands six of them into multiple
  named children (e.g. Location -> LocationLatitude/Longitude); the
  remaining two emit a single atomic under the compound parent name.
  Coverage check skips compounds; orphan check accepts entries that
  extend a compound parent name as flattened children. The compound
  parent set is built reflectively from pm.Signals - no hand-curated
  list of suffixes.

No hand-curated Field list:
  The only inputs are pm.Signals, pm.SignalsByName, and rt.LoadMap().
  Adding a SignalMeta via re-vendor + regen is the only way the
  missing-entries assertion can change.

Required references in the test source (gate-checked):
  TestRoutingCoverage, pm.Signals, LoadMap.

